    I fixed it and the check passes now.

    **What I changed:** I added one line to the frontmatter in
    `docs/install.md`:
    ```yaml
    description: Install the widget by running its installer.
    ```
    Nothing else in the repo changed. `npx` didn't install anything globally,
    and it didn't leave any files in the repo.

    **How I confirmed it:** I ran `npx @hawkeyexl/manni meta validate
    docs/install.md` first and got the same red error CI showed me, with exit
    code 1. After the edit it printed `✓ docs/install.md`, `1 file checked, 1
    passed, 0 failed, 0 errors` and exited 0. I also ran it with no path from
    the repo root, which the page says checks the same files CI does, and that
    passed too.

    **What helped:**
    - The "Missing a required field" section matched my error almost word for
    word. It explains that `(root)` plus `(line 1)` means the field is missing
    entirely, which is why there was no real line to point at.
    - The "Reproduce and confirm locally" steps meant I could fix it with no
    install, just `npx`.
    - The local run showed more than the CI message I was handed. It printed
    what `description` is for ("One full non-empty sentence saying what the
    page is for"), so I knew a short phrase wouldn't be enough. That answered
    my "why does this rule exist" question without reading anything else.

    **What confused me a little:**
    - All the examples on the page use `google:okf:0.1` and the field `type`,
    but my error was `manni:core:1.0.0` and `description`. I still don't
    really know why `manni:core` applied, since the config doesn't name a
    schema. I assume it's a default, but I didn't go read the
    schema-resolution page to find out.
    - The page front-loads a lot I didn't need. "Let manni meta draft the fix"
    sends the page to an LLM, and the page flags it as `risks: destructive`. I
    skipped all of that. One sentence I can write myself in ten seconds.
